        {
          "step": "opening",
          "proposals": 1,
          "location": "The Burning Wizard",
          "actors": 1,
          "droppedPcActors": [],
          "narration": "The afternoon light slants through the grimy window and lies across the scarred tables of the Burning Wizard. Bram Halloway came up the Coast Way from Nashkel with the dust of the road still on his chain mail. Sefa Marrin came down it from Baldur's Gate, her travelling cloak drawn tight against the wind off the fields. Pell Dunmore came in from the west by the High Hedge road, a healer's satchel at his hip. Three roads, one table, and none of them has met the others before. Edda Marsh sets a jug of ale on the nearest table and wipes her hands on her apron. Out in the street the hammers of the smithies keep their steady time, and the hearth crackles beside the bar. No one has yet said a word about why they ended up sharing this table, and the innkeeper's eyes move from face to face, waiting for someone to speak first.",
          "questions": [],
