        {
          "step": "opening",
          "proposals": 1,
          "location": "The Mouth of the Ruin below Beregost",
          "actors": 0,
          "droppedPcActors": [],
          "narration": "Sefa Marrin, Pell Dunmore and Bram Halloway stand together at the edge of the ruin, a day's ride from Beregost, with the afternoon sun at their backs. Worn stone steps run down into a dark that the daylight does not reach. Cold air rises from below, carrying a dry, old smell, and somewhere far beneath them something scrapes across stone, then falls silent as if listening. Behind them the trail winds back through the trees, open and clear. Each of them faces the same choice: to go down, to wait at the threshold, or to turn back the way they came. The sound comes again, and this time it seems a little nearer. What does the company do?",
          "questions": [],
          "startMinutes": 840
